HILLTOP BOOSTER PS-3 SURGE (WATER HAMMER) STUDY - 2019
PUBLIC SUMMARY / EXECUTIVE SUMMARY ONLY
Prepared for {{ ww_org_name }} by Hydra Controls Integration LLC with
Brandt & Lowe Engineers.  Final report dated 2019-09-30.

Purpose
  Evaluate hydraulic transients on the 16" transmission main between the
  Cedar Ridge WTP and Hilltop PS-3 / Summit Tank after the 2018 pump upgrade.

Key findings
  1. Fast closure of flow control valve FCV-301 (or a sudden stop of both
     booster pumps) can produce pressure surges well above normal operating
     pressure. The critical period of the line is roughly 7 seconds.
  2. The weakest point on the main is the 1962 cast-iron Miller Creek
     crossing.
  3. With the recommended protections in place, predicted surge pressures
     stay within the rating of all pipe segments.

Recommendations (implemented 2020)
  - Limit FCV-301 closure rate in RTU logic (valve slew-rate limit).
  - Install and keep ARMED surge anticipator valve SAV-301 at PS-3.
  - Keep the pump high-discharge-pressure trip in service.
  - Replace the Miller Creek crossing (FY29 capital plan).

  In short: valve closure rate limits and SAV-301 protect the 1962
  cast-iron Miller Creek crossing.

Detailed calculations, transient model files and RTU setpoint justification
are on the engineering workstation (ww-eng01), not on this share.
